ive.\n\n3. **Calculate the squares of these integers:**\n   \\[\n   4^2 = 16 \\quad \\text{(ends in 6)}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   5^2 = 25 \\quad \\text{(does not end in 6)}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   6^2 = 36 \\quad \\text{(ends in 6)}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   7^2 = 49 \\quad \\text{(does not end in 6)}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   8^2 = 64 \\quad \\text{(does not end in 6)}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   9^2 = 81 \\quad \\text{(does not end in 6)}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Identify the values of $B$ for the numbers that end in 6:**\n   - For $16$, $B = 1$.\n   - For $36$, $B = 3$.\n\n5. **Count the distinct values of $B$:**\n   - The distinct values of $B$ are 1 and 3.\n\nThus, there are $\\boxed{2}$ distinct possible values for $B$."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
